# Pack snapshots and their patch pairs are hashed, and several tests pin those
# hashes, so what git checks out has to be byte-for-byte what was committed.
# End-of-line translation would silently change them.
* -text

# This does not reach everywhere. Eighteen vendored packs ship their own
# `.gitattributes` — usually `* text=auto` — and a nested file wins over this
# one for its own subtree. That is upstream's file, part of the snapshot, so it
# is left alone rather than edited to suit us.
#
# The consequence is one file: AIGODLIKE-COMFYUI-TRANSLATION declares
# `eol=crlf`, so its `v2/comfy-api.pyi` is checked out with CRLF and hashes
# differently than the copy that was committed. Every other pinned artifact —
# the other 67 stubs and all 69 patch pairs — resolves to `eol: unspecified`
# and round-trips exactly.
#
# ComfyUI_secure_nodes carries the same defect for the same reason; this is
# inherited, not introduced. Fixing it means neutralising the vendored
# attributes files, which is a change to snapshot fidelity and wants its own
# decision.
